class:: FFTPhaseDev2
summary:: Wrapped second phase difference
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/FFTFlux2, Classes/FFTComplexDev2

description::
Mean or sum of absolute wrapped second phase differences. Weighted mode multiplies by current magnitude. Histories advance for every bin, including bins below the magnitude gate, so low-energy bins cannot misalign the phase history. Independently implemented from Dixon, Onset Detection Revisited (DAFx 2006).

DC and Nyquist are excluded from the evidence; normalization includes their two positions in the bin count. Raw FFT magnitudes are used without window or FFT-size compensation. The first two valid frames output zero while the phase predictor warms up. Results hold between FFT frames. Persistent storage is allocated at construction; the FFT buffer is read without modifying its representation. Like vanilla Onsets, this exposes spectral onset evidence, but it has no peak picking. Use Onsets2 for triggers.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
An FFT chain with the declared size.
argument:: weighted
Positive multiplies each phase difference by its bin magnitude.
argument:: normalize
Positive divides by the one-sided bin count.
argument:: floor
Positive weak-bin magnitude gate, default 1e-6.
argument:: fftSize
Literal matching FFT size, a power of two from 256 through 8192.
returns::
One nonnegative control-rate evidence value.

examples::
FFTPhaseDev2 computes the second difference of spectral phase, highlighting sudden phase discontinuities caused by percussive attacks. In this example, it drives an adaptive pitch-flutter modulator: phase jumps trigger sudden tape-style micro-pitch fluctuations across an auxiliary delay line on acoustic drums. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: tracks the real-time phase deviation evidence.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var dev = FFTPhaseDev2.kr(chain, weighted: 1, fftSize: 1024);
        var flutter = dev.lag(0.02) * 0.004;
        var delay = DelayC.ar(source, 0.05, 0.01 + flutter) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + delay;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, dev) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Phase Deviation", ~miraBus, 0.0, 3.14);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
